1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:11,875
A factory checks every product on the line before it ships. CI CD does the same for code: every change is tested and deployed automatically.

2
00:00:12,570 --> 00:00:18,070
If a test fails, the line stops, and nothing broken reaches customers.

3
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:27,280
Every push runs the same steps: install, test, build, and deploy, only if everything passed.

4
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:34,580
CDM Studio itself works this way: every change is tested before it goes live.

5
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:44,055
Small, frequent releases are safer than one giant release, like small steps instead of a big jump.

6
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:48,035
And always have a quick way to roll back.

